    "release_notes": "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/feature/tarkir-dragonstorm-release-notes",
    "cost_rule_correction": "CR118.11/12: legal replacement-modified payment remains paid; true prohibition/no legal resource prevents paying.",
    "unpreventable_inference": "CR615.1 describes prevention effects as shields;615.8 uses an actual prevented instance as the exhaustion point;615.12/12a applies once to unpreventable damage without reducing the shield. Therefore preserve this effect without a reflexive trigger on actual prevented0. Root independently concurred. Official TDM notes have no specific lifetime ruling.",
    "xmage_discrepancies": [
      "TargetSource includes unreferenced graveyard/exile objects; use609.7a semantic source universe instead.",
      "PreventionEffectImpl.applies requires DamageEvent.preventable, so XMage skips rather than applies once for unpreventable damage. This also leaves the effect unconsumed, but CR615.12a is modeled explicitly here."
    ]
  },
  "implementation": [
    "EffectChoiceKind::DiscardHand samples and discards the actual whole current hand after mana children, with empty hand payable. It reuses ordinary additional-cost payment and ordered speculative departure projection. It is scoped to ordinary activation cost, not generic LED-style mana-ability additional costs.",
    "Source-prevention state is boxed under existing cold RoleState. Choice is chooser-private, shields public, effect independent of source departure. Captured physical permanent spells follow their exact Stack->BF continuation; copies and later reentry are distinct.",
    "Affected player chooses prevention/replacement order; actual positive prevented amount and damage-time source controller are frozen in a normal independently counterable reflexive trigger. Zero/unpreventable/global-ban/other-effect prevention boundaries tested separately.",
    "Simultaneous duplicate source/recipient fragments with identical frozen source/combat/preventability are combined before replacement selection, giving one next-instance prevention total and one reflexive trigger.",
    "Mass-copy layer provider and hand-size clocks now share one creation timestamp while acquisition origins remain independent. Ordinary single-copy consumers retain their prior chronology."
  ],
